{"resourceIdentifier":"5108","resourceName":"Bamboo King Vina Biochar Project","description":"The Bamboo King Vina Biochar Project aims to address the substantial waste generated from bamboo and wood processing at the Bamboo King Vina (BKV) factory in Lang Chanh district, Thanh Hoa province, Vietnam. The factory, with a daily processing capacity of 1,500 tons, generates approximately 800-900 tons of waste per day. To mitigate this environmental impact, the project will install and operate six biochar production facilities using pyrolysis technology. This process converts bamboo and wood waste into biochar, a carbon-rich material.\r\nThe produced biochar will be applied directly to soil or used indirectly in agricultural land through animal feed, livestock bedding, sludge management, composting, or anaerobic digestion. The project's objectives include reducing bamboo waste sent to landfills or left to decay, which contributes to greenhouse gas emissions. Utilizing biochar in soil management aims to enhance agricultural land, promote carbon-rich ecosystems, improve crop yields, and boost food security. Additionally, it seeks to foster healthier communities and economic prosperity for local at-risk populations.","location":{"latitude":20.167000,"longitude":105.167000},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2024-06-11","endExclusive":"2024-07-12","endInclusive":"2024-07-11"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"5108"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Thanh Hoa"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Bamboo King Vina Joint Stock Company"},{"type":"string","value":"Thanh Hoa Province, Viet Nam"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"44634"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NA